{
  "notes": [
    "The V3 commit binds only the Verifier value root and salt, not the reveal payload hash.",
    "The V3 result signature binds the Verifier value root, metric leaf count and zero plaintext encryption commitment.",
    "The V2 reveal payload retains a separate integrity digest and includes the InferReceiptV3 digest.",
    "metric_summary_v1_zero_leaves is a result with no metric leaves (a legal zero-token output): every numeric field is 0, each enabled optional ratio is present(0) and every count is 0; the sample is judged PASS with count 0.",
    "metric_summary_v1_worker_values_missing has three leaves whose Worker values are all missing: no comparison may read as agreement, so each enabled comparison takes its worst value (abs logprob diff mean/p95/p99 4294967295, rank-delta rate 1000000, top-K Jaccard present(0), union JS present(1000000)) and both compared counts are 0; the sample is rejected against the Worker.",
    "When there are no comparable leaves and a position has a finite Worker value but a missing or non-finite Verifier value, the Verifier cannot attribute the empty sample and publishes no summary (a Verifier execution failure, treated as a missed reveal), so that case has no vector. With at least one comparable leaf, missing positions count in missing_compared_count."
  ],
